# The built package is a build artifact, not source. build.ps1 regenerates it.
#
# Deliberate, and it is a change from RS_Reload's convention: all six source
# repos track their own pk3/zip, and that is a live hazard for THIS repo
# specifically -- staging a committed artifact from any of them would put a
# complete copy of a mod inside the merged pk3, which is a duplicate-class
# fatal. The packer uses an explicit include list so it cannot happen by
# accident; not tracking the output means it cannot happen on purpose either.
#
# RS_WeaponWheel is the closest call of the six: it keeps RS_WeaponWheel.pk3
# in its repo root, one level ABOVE the package directory its lane points at.
# Two things independently stop it being staged -- the lane path, and the fact
# that stage.ps1 only ever reads *.zs plus the four asset subdirectories.
*.pk3
*.zip

# Local agent config. RS_Holsters shipped this file inside its distributed
# archive; it is not source and it is not content.
.claude/

__pycache__/

# Engine logs and diagnostic captures, written next to whatever launched the
# build. Never source. Globbed rather than listed because each new one is
# named after whatever was being chased that day -- log-netcvarflood.txt was
# the third to turn up untracked.
doomxr-log.txt
log-*.txt
